    "body": "Small fixes to stale argument metadata and help text in the wallet RPCs:\n\n- listtransactions: the \"Negative from\" error references the skip argument by its old name\n- listsinceblock: name the failing argument when target_confirmations < 1 instead of a bare \"Invalid parameter\"\n- sendmany: the help examples pass values in the minconf position, which is an ignored dummy; describe what the example actually sets and pass null for the ignored placeholder\n- getbalance: add the (DEPRECATED) marker to include_watchonly, matching the identical argument in six other RPCs\n- send: include_watching used a string default \"false\" on a BOOL argument, rendering as default=\"false\" in the help; adds help metadata coverage\n\nTests updated in wallet_listtransactions, wallet_listsinceblock, and wallet_send (new assertion that include_watching renders as a bool with a bool default).",
